{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1154795-a-question-regarding-nwo-syndicate-civil-war-metaplot","id":1154795,"title":"A question regarding NWO-Syndicate civil war metaplot","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-01T12:11:53-07:00","id":1154795,"title":"A question regarding NWO-Syndicate civil war metaplot","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But instead of accepting that they\u2019re really two Conventions in one, NWO is grabbing at more power. <i><b>They\u2019re taking direct control of manufacturing Iteration X and Progenitor war assets.</b> </i>Hell, they\u2019re even going as far as capturing Traditionalists and Processing them to send against their own kind. </div> </div> </div>Does it mean besides the Atlas Project, NWO is actively taking over production of military installations and war factories of TM Managers and Macrotechnicians with permission of Iteration X?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11780,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","user":"Posthumanity","date":". 11-01-2017, 03:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T12:37:33-07:00","id":1154807,"title":"","content":"Well, NWO it's in very good terms with ItX. With their mastery of mind they're good at training (and process) the soldiers created by these conventions. And they're working together in the project to attach Awakened Avatars to HitMarks to create terminator mages. Perhaps that's what they mean with &quot;war assets&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T16:48:54-07:00","id":1154883,"title":"","content":"Iteration X has always been the 'War' convention. They might build things, and build them well. But culturally, what they are really formed for, and really all about is kicking down doors and killing everyone inside the apartment to get at one guy. Then bombing the building to rubble just to be sure if they're allowed. Every possible vector of assault will be considered.<br /> <br /> They build things to make themselves more perfect, and their definition of perfection has always had to do with raw physical power and the capacity to predict the world around them so as to use that power effectively.<br /> <br /> All the NWO really has to do to take Direct Control is give them an enemy to fight. And Iteration X is theirs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T04:42:12-07:00","id":1155348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1154795-a-question-regarding-nwo-syndicate-civil-war-metaplot#post1154795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does it mean besides the Atlas Project, NWO is actively taking over production of military installations and war factories of TM Managers and Macrotechnicians with permission of Iteration X?</div> </div> </div> </div>This suggest this; but the permission of the Iteration-X in regards to this is not mentioned. The New World Order of the Technocracy would probably be using their influence within the Technocracy to do this; rather than asking for the Iteration-X 's permission.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T10:44:30-07:00","id":1155443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1154795-a-question-regarding-nwo-syndicate-civil-war-metaplot?p=1154807#post1154807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, NWO it's in very good terms with ItX. With their mastery of mind they're good at training (and process) the soldiers created by these conventions. And they're working together in the project to attach Awakened Avatars to HitMarks to create terminator mages. Perhaps that's what they mean with &quot;war assets&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't Atlas an independent project of NWO, implemented without consent, support or assistance from ItX?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T11:49:53-07:00","id":1155467,"title":"","content":"I assumed that ItX would be involved since HitMarks are their thing. It's stated that they aren't?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T13:54:30-07:00","id":1155518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1154795-a-question-regarding-nwo-syndicate-civil-war-metaplot?p=1155467#post1155467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assumed that ItX would be involved since HitMarks are their thing. It's stated that they aren't?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, when ItX abandoned their HitMarks program, NWO took over it and converted it into the Enlightened Shock Corps, a.k.a Atlas. They also took control over the few constructs that have left away from ItX, without their permission.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T09:46:55-07:00","id":1155757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1154795-a-question-regarding-nwo-syndicate-civil-war-metaplot?p=1154883#post1154883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Iteration X has always been the 'War' convention. They might build things, and build them well. But culturally, what they are really formed for, and really all about is kicking down doors and killing everyone inside the apartment to get at one guy. Then bombing the building to rubble just to be sure if they're allowed. Every possible vector of assault will be considered.<br /> <br /> They build things to make themselves more perfect, and their definition of perfection has always had to do with raw physical power and the capacity to predict the world around them so as to use that power effectively.<br /> <br /> All the NWO really has to do to take Direct Control is give them an enemy to fight. And Iteration X is theirs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always saw it as It-X being more about being the &quot;Building Shit&quot; Convention. And wars are a great way to inspire and test new innovations. But not the only way and It-X is just as busy doing those things. And their hierarchical nature makes them very efficient at assuming a military posture (But they're efficient at most things, since they actually have a self-criticism Methodology specifically tasked with improving efficiency). But being the best at prosecuting war doesn't necessarily make them warlike. Both the NWO and the Syndicate seem more concerned with provoking conflicts and then drawing in others to do some (most?) of the front line fighting....<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T21:35:56-07:00","id":1155941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1154795-a-question-regarding-nwo-syndicate-civil-war-metaplot?p=1155757#post1155757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always saw it as It-X being more about being the &quot;Building Shit&quot; Convention. And wars are a great way to inspire and test new innovations. But not the only way and It-X is just as busy doing those things. And their hierarchical nature makes them very efficient at assuming a military posture (But they're efficient at most things, since they actually have a self-criticism Methodology specifically tasked with improving efficiency). But being the best at prosecuting war doesn't necessarily make them warlike. Both the NWO and the Syndicate seem more concerned with provoking conflicts and then drawing in others to do some (most?) of the front line fighting....</div> </div> </div> </div>And I think NWO also do love well-defined, clear, efficient hierarchy and jurisdiction as much as It-X, especially the Operatives. They are definitely the most &quot;orderly&quot; Convention along with It-X, and with the exception of Collegia, they brook no delay or argument. And in the Union, that <i>says </i>something...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11780,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","user":"Posthumanity","date":". 11-05-2017, 12:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T22:36:46-07:00","id":1155955,"title":"","content":"The NWO is also full of psychologists, logicians, and information analysts. Which means they are superb at convincing people why they should do something. (The Syndicate has the opposite advantage: YOU have to convince THEM why they should give you money). When the NWO talks with the strictly logical Iteration X, it's easy for them to see eye to eye.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T07:27:42-08:00","id":1156042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1154795-a-question-regarding-nwo-syndicate-civil-war-metaplot?p=1155955#post1155955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The NWO is also full of psychologists, logicians, and information analysts. Which means they are superb at convincing people why they should do something. (The Syndicate has the opposite advantage: YOU have to convince THEM why they should give you money). When the NWO talks with the strictly logical Iteration X, it's easy for them to see eye to eye.</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as it's more on the MiB side than the Ivory Tower folks... <br /> <br /> Uber-academia is a status-obsessed nest of incestuous vipers that doesn't bear the faintest resemblance to something logical or orderly. Admittedly the powers that be in the Ivory Tower know that, are masters of applied psychology/sociology/anthropology and know to use the MiBs as their stalking horse. Or is that more false-flag? Perhaps even Judas goat?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T08:25:10-08:00","id":1156060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1154795-a-question-regarding-nwo-syndicate-civil-war-metaplot?p=1155757#post1155757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I always saw it as It-X being more about being the &quot;Building Shit&quot; Convention. And wars are a great way to inspire and test new innovations. But not the only way and It-X is just as busy doing those things. And their hierarchical nature makes them very efficient at assuming a military posture (But they're efficient at most things, since they actually have a self-criticism Methodology specifically tasked with improving efficiency). But being the best at prosecuting war doesn't necessarily make them warlike. Both the NWO and the Syndicate seem more concerned with provoking conflicts and then drawing in others to do some (most?) of the front line fighting....</div> </div> </div> </div>Except their entire characterization in revised was &quot;The Convention built for War without a proper War to fight, and is thus now finally able to take their gaze away from the enemy immediately in front of them and look around at the big picture.&quot;<br /> <br /> And prior to that, their characterization was more or less all about how only the technocracy was strong enough to control ascension, and they were going to prove it by beating every non-technocrats skull in.<br /> <br /> I always saw the 'good at building shit' as a side effect of Iteration X effectively being the 'standing military' branch of the earth-bound Technocracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T13:07:37-08:00","id":1156144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1154795-a-question-regarding-nwo-syndicate-civil-war-metaplot?p=1156060#post1156060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except their entire characterization in revised was &quot;The Convention built for War without a proper War to fight, and is thus now finally able to take their gaze away from the enemy immediately in front of them and look around at the big picture.&quot;<br /> <br /> And prior to that, their characterization was more or less all about how only the technocracy was strong enough to control ascension, and they were going to prove it by beating every non-technocrats skull in.<br /> <br /> I always saw the 'good at building shit' as a side effect of Iteration X effectively being the 'standing military' branch of the earth-bound Technocracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you actually have anything remotely like a &quot;standing military&quot; for a faction of mages? I mean, maybe proxy fights and some direct action by the equivalent of spec-ops, but a standing military is a completely different thing. <br /> <br /> The original slant on It-X was just as poor as the original slant on all the other Conventions, as they were just deep dives into the antagonist mindset to flesh them out when everyone knows the REAL game is about the Traditions. Since then every other Convention has been fleshed out to something that makes sense in line with actual mission of the Technocracy. Which is no longer focused on the Pogrom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}